 # IP Address Manager (full stack)
 
 Track which device uses which IP address, detect conflicts, and see free addresses on a subnet map.
+Every person registers and logs in, and sees only **their own** devices.
 
 - **Frontend:** React + Vite (`client/`)
 - **Backend:** Node.js REST API (`server/`), built-in `http` and `node:sqlite`, no npm packages needed
@@ -22,6 +23,14 @@ Node.js **22.13 or newer** (`node -v` to check). Node 22 prints an "experimental
 
 Open http://localhost:5173.
 
+## Accounts
+- **Register** with a username (3-30 letters, numbers, `.` `-` `_`) and a password of at least 8 characters.
+- **Log in** to see your own devices. Two people can use the same IP address in their own lists without clashing.
+- **Log out** with the button at the top right. Logging out ends the session on the server too.
+- Sessions last 7 days.
+
+**Upgrading from the version without accounts:** the old `server/data.db` has no owner for its devices, so the server discards the old device table on first start. If you see any database error, stop the server and delete `server/data.db`, then start again.
+
